WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.690
Twitter bots are such a big deal that Elon
Musk put his Twitter purchase on hold just

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.001
to figure out how many bots or fake accounts
exist on Twitter.

00:00:08.001 --> 00:00:09.001
He put the deal on hold in mid-May to figure
out if Twitter was underreporting the number

00:00:09.001 --> 00:00:10.001
of fake accounts on its platform.

00:00:10.001 --> 00:00:12.160
Fake accounts pretend to be someone else or
are automated accounts that don’t have a

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.630
real person behind them that can do things
like real humans can do: send out tweets,

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:17.800
like, and retweet.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:22.070
There’s apparently even a market for fake
Elon Musk Twitter accounts!

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:27.789
This is important because it is the number
of real users that determines the value of

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:28.789
Twitter.

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:33.820
So if Twitter’s 229 million daily active
users are not 229 million real human beings,

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.770
then Musk argues the company's value is less
than the $44 billion he’s agreed to pay

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:38.770
for it.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:39.770
Musk decided it wasn’t worth it to buy Twitter
for $44 billion because its 229 million daily

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:40.770
active users don’t represent 229 million
real human beings.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.270
Musk tweeted that 20% of Twitter consists
of fake or spam accounts, though he didn’t

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.600
cite any sources.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.850
That contradicts Twitter’s claim that fewer
than 5% of accounts on its platform are fake.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.240
Musk says he wants Twitter’s CEO Parag Agrawal
to show proof.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.830
And that the “deal cannot move forward until
he does.”

00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:00.990
That wording is much stronger than his previous
tweet that he was “still committed to acquisition”

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.100
hours after putting the deal on hold.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.429
When Musk appeared on the All-In-Podcast in
May, he again questioned Twitter’s claim

00:01:07.429 --> 00:01:10.109
that less than 5% of its accounts are fake.

00:01:10.109 --> 00:01:15.070
Said another way, the number of real-unique
humans that you see making comments on a daily

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:20.200
basis on Twitter is above 95%, that is what
they’re claiming.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.060
Does anyone have that experience?

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:29.175
Hahahahaha

00:01:29.175 --> 00:01:33.035
HAHAHAHAHA

00:01:33.035 --> 00:01:35.380
Really?

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.679
There’s a bridge I’d like to sell you, y'know.

00:01:39.679 --> 00:01:42.909
He also likened his agreement to purchase
Twitter to agreeing to buy a home that the

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:45.950
homeowner said had only 5% termites.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.600
Only to later realize it’s infested.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.040
And the whole deal may need to be reconsidered.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.570
A software company found the number of fake
or spam accounts is four times higher than

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:56.950
Twitter’s estimate.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.969
SparkToro analyzed profile pictures, location
data, and used machine learning processes

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:06.170
to conclude 19% Twitter accounts are fake
or spam.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.509
Larger accounts are even harder hit.

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:14.170
SparkToro said 43% of Joe Biden’s Twitter
followers on his personal @JoeBiden account

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:15.659
are fake and inactive.

00:02:15.659 --> 00:02:22.260
It’s even higher for Elon Musk: the company
says 70% of his followers are fake and inactive.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:25.960
Why does the number of fake and spam accounts
matter so much?

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:29.680
Someone who wants to manipulate public opinion
could create hundreds of fake accounts to

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.879
criticize a policy or a politician to influence
how you vote, hype a product to control what

00:02:34.879 --> 00:02:39.120
you buy, or, make someone seem more or less
popular than they really are.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.620
A cybersecurity researcher believes bots are
responsible for what he calls the attempted

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.569
character assassination of Elon Musk.

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:51.140
Andrea Stroppa notes they’ve been tweeting
out “Elongate SpaceX scandal” in reference

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:56.380
to the SpaceX flight attendant who has accused
Musk of sexual assault, which Musk denies.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:01.739
They’re not just interacting with Musk’s
critics but also his fans….so that conversations

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:06.170
can reach a wider audience rather than the
“echo chamber” of Musk haters.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:10.340
Fake and spam accounts are influencing public
discourse inauthentically as they don’t

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:11.870
represent the views of real people.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:16.959
There are things you and I can do to try to
remove bots from our feed.

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:21.629
Stroppa suggests muting some of your Twitter
notifications….for example, from people

00:03:21.629 --> 00:03:25.240
who don’t have a profile picture, or who
haven’t confirmed their e-mail address or

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:26.550
phone number.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:31.000
Musk said one of his top priorities after
taking over Twitter is to defeat spambots

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:37.140
and authenticate all humans, which would dwindle
his followers from 94 million down to 28 million

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:42.739
if it’s really true 70% of his followers
are fake or spam.

00:03:42.739 --> 00:03:48.409
But whenever there are fans you can bet there
are critics.

00:03:48.409 --> 00:03:52.450
Many liberals have been outraged over Musk’s
push for more free speech on Twitter, which

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:54.010
he believes is being stifled.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:57.790
For example, he said he’d reverse the platform’s
ban on Trump.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:00.709
Conservatives have long-accused Twitter of
censoring their views.

00:04:00.709 --> 00:04:05.609
A Twitter employee recently confirmed the
apparent left-leaning bias at the company.

00:04:05.609 --> 00:04:09.859
This senior engineer was caught in a secret
recording by the right-wing activist organization

00:04:09.859 --> 00:04:15.060
Project Veritas saying Twitter does not believe
in free speech, and admitted some of his colleagues

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.329
“hate” Musk’s purchase because they’re
“super left”

00:04:18.329 --> 00:04:22.870
Another employee also recorded by Project
Veritas made it clear Twitter is not ONLY

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:27.310
about free speech and then proceeded to make
fun of Musk because of his Asperger’s, calling

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:30.000
him “literally special needs”.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.360
Not that poking fun at him would get under
his skin, or criticism of any kind.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.840
Musk said during a TED Talk interview this
year that criticism for his billionaire status

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.120
was “water off a duck’s back”.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:45.669
He’s a man on a mission to deal with bots
and issues of free speech.

00:04:45.669 --> 00:04:50.030
If for some reason the Twitter deal doesn’t
end up going through, he could still be a

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:51.710
social media mogul.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:54.070
He mentioned he’s considered starting his
own app.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:57.740
We’ve imagined it might be called Elon Social.

